{
  "cdmVersionRange": ">=5.0.0",
  "_README": ["Coronary artery disease - the Kraiss sVQI-FS cad item (1 point).", "ALIGNED 2026-11-01 WITH OHDSI PHENOTYPE LIBRARY ENTRY 197 ('Coronary Artery Disease from vessel disease to ischemic injury') per workspace Rule 1 (use the published phenotype unless there is a clear analytic reason to deviate). Concept set = PL 197's roots + descendants, EXCEPT its root 318443 'Arteriosclerotic vascular disease', which is replaced by its coronary branch 317576 'Coronary arteriosclerosis'.", "WHY THE ONE DEVIATION: 318443 spans every vascular bed (aortic, carotid, renal, upper/lower-limb and limb bypass-graft atherosclerosis; 95 concepts reached only through it, none cardiac). In a PAD amputation cohort that would label nearly every patient as having coronary disease. The 82 concepts this set adds over the earlier 4185932-only version are all coronary or myocardial-infarction related; the earlier set missed coronary arteriosclerosis / coronary atherosclerosis (e.g. ICD-10 I25.10) entirely, and Duke prevalence was 21 percent (124 of 587).", "Five other PL 197 roots are NOT carried: 319038 and 45766212 are deprecated in the vocabulary (no mapping, no descendants) and 4058723 / 4177223 / 44809539 (H/O angina, H/O PTCA, H/O acute coronary syndrome) are non-standard and map only to the generic 'History of event' (1340204), which cannot define coronary disease.", "Both a ConditionOccurrence and an Observation criterion are used, as in PL 197 (the emergency-admission concept is Observation-domain). covariates/covariate_concepts_vqifs.csv :: cad lists the same roots and its domain is 'auto'.", "Replaces the reused Limit=First [DVI] VA-FI Coronary artery disease cohort 1797949.", "PrimaryCriteriaLimit / QualifiedLimit / ExpressionLimit are all \"All\" and EndStrategy is StartDate+0, unlike the [DVI] VA-FI cohorts (1797948-1797977) which are \"First\". A first-ever-only cohort cannot answer a lookback-window question."],
